[lesson]   Solution: FIX_PLAN: ;  1. Export PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True in quantize_wrapper.sh (reduces fragmentation, as the OOM error itself suggests);  2. Pass --seqlen 1024 from the wrapper (halves calibration activation memory ≈ 830 MB saved + proportional MXFP8 temp reduction; safe for MXFP8 accuracy);  Keep nsamples=128 (128 samples is needed for representative MXFP8 calibration; only per-sample memory matters, and seqlen reduction already covers that);
[lesson] Saved: [fixed] torch.OutOfMemoryError: CUDA out of memory. Tried to allocate 160.00 MiB. GPU 0 
